## Context

Surfaced during ticket 0572 execution (PR #1042): regenerating
`tab_exp2_wiki_compliance.csv` from the current parser does not reproduce
the committed artifact — anthropic naive run4 `n_cells_s1s2` flips 0→148
on re-parse. The artifact was committed by ticket 0452; either the parser
changed since, or the committed value was produced by a different code
path. PR #1042 restored the committed version; the mismatch itself is
unresolved. This breaks the "committed artifacts re-derive from the
pipeline" reproducibility contract.

## Actions

1. Reproduce: rerun the generating script and diff against the committed
   CSV; isolate which parse step produces the 0→148 flip.
2. Decide which value is correct (inspect the raw run output for
   anthropic naive run4); fix the parser or regenerate the artifact —
   fix the master, never patch downstream.
3. Add a regression guard if the defect class is testable.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Regenerating tab_exp2_wiki_compliance.csv reproduces the committed
  file byte-identically (or the committed file is updated with a
  documented correction)
- [ ] `make check` passes
